1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,957
Can you throw away receipts after 3 years?

2
00:00:03,257 --> 00:00:04,335
Often, yes.

3
00:00:04,335 --> 00:00:06,140
But it’s 3 years from when you file.

4
00:00:06,140 --> 00:00:07,352
Not from when you bought it.

5
00:00:07,802 --> 00:00:10,119
A receipt from March 2026

6
00:00:10,119 --> 00:00:13,535
goes on the return you file in April 2027.

7
00:00:13,535 --> 00:00:16,417
Keep it until at least April 2030.

8
00:00:16,867 --> 00:00:18,195
Now the exceptions.

9
00:00:18,195 --> 00:00:19,851
Equipment? Keep that receipt

10
00:00:19,851 --> 00:00:21,149
until the clock runs out

11
00:00:21,149 --> 00:00:22,511
on the year you sell it.

12
00:00:22,811 --> 00:00:24,815
Left out more than a quarter of your income?

13
00:00:24,815 --> 00:00:25,865
Six years.

14
00:00:25,865 --> 00:00:27,806
Never filed? Keep everything.

15
00:00:28,256 --> 00:00:29,805
So clean out by tax year.

16
00:00:29,805 --> 00:00:31,698
Never by the date on the receipt.

17
00:00:32,198 --> 00:00:34,155
Find us at receipt-nest.com,

18
00:00:34,155 --> 00:00:35,896
on the App Store and Google Play.
